CORE
main.py
--unwind 3

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[python-attribute-error\.\d+\] .*'Sub' object has no attribute 'x' \(AttributeError\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
differential2 §11 inheritance. The AttributeError analysis follows the
inheritance chain: a bare-annotation field is "definitely assigned"
for a subclass only if the subclass assigns it or calls
super().__init__() onto a base that does. Sub omits super().__init__(),
so the inherited x is unassigned and reading s.x is an AttributeError.
